        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "40968ca2-60b5-5ec1-94d4-889b3eb4e07b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Queens, Staten Island, Flushing Meadows–Corona Park, Queens County\n- Systems: I-678, Van Wyck Expressway, Grand Central Parkway, LaGuardia Airport\n- Concepts: population, area, foreign-born residents\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1899, the borough of Queens has been coterminous with Queens County.\n- In 2016, Queens had a census-estimated population of 2,333,054, making it the second-largest New York City borough by population after Brooklyn.\n- In 2016, approximately 48% of Queens residents were foreign-born.\n- In 2016, Staten Island had a census-estimated population of 476,015, making it the least populated New York City borough.\n- Staten Island is the third-largest New York City borough by area at 58 square miles.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park is located in the borough of Queens.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park lies between I-678, also called the Van Wyck Expressway, and the Grand Central Parkway.\n- Flushing Meadows–Corona Park stretches from Flushing Bay at the southern edge of LaGuardia Airport to Union Turnpike.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "dbc1d292-c6a2-556b-af48-a8064c69197c",
        "text": "Page: Queens. Sentence: Coterminous with Queens County since 1899, the borough of Queens is the second-largest in population (after Brooklyn), with a census-estimated 2,333,054 residents in 2016, approximately 48% of them foreign-born.\nPage: Staten Island. Sentence: With a 2016 Census-estimated population of 476,015, Staten Island is the least populated of the boroughs but is the third-largest in area at 58 sqmi .\nPage: Flushing Meadows–Corona Park. Sentence: Located in the borough of Queens, it is between I-678 (Van Wyck Expressway) and the Grand Central Parkway and stretches from Flushing Bay, at the southern edge of LaGuardia Airport, to Union Turnpike.",
